<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
<!--
Hardened runtime (codesign --options runtime, citadel#672) blocks a process
from sending Apple Events to other apps unless this entitlement is present --
independent of App Sandbox, which this bundle does not use.
packaging/macos/citadel-launcher drives Terminal.app via `osascript` to open a
window and run the CLI; that is the bundle's only current use of Apple Events,
and it silently breaks the moment hardened runtime signing lands without this
entry.

NOTE: this comment must stay AFTER the closing </plist> tag. codesign's
entitlements parser (AMFIUnserializeXML) is stricter than plutil/libxml: a
comment placed before <plist>, or nested inside <dict>, both pass
`plutil -lint` but make codesign fail with "AMFIUnserializeXML: syntax error"
at sign time. Verified empirically while wiring this file in -- there is no
public Apple documentation of the restriction. Only a trailing comment, after
</plist>, is safe.
-->
